The parameter on the projection layer must be a subset of the respective parameter on the base layer, meaning
it can have the same or less components as the one on the base layer. Fields or associations that are defined as
mandatory on the base layer must be part of the parameter on the projection layer.
Components of parameters on the projection layer can have a different name than the ones on the base layer.
Their type, however, needs to be compatible. The relation to the corresponding components on the base layer
must be specified using respective mapping instructions in the abstract behavior definition projection. This is
necessary for every component of the projection layer parameter, even if their name does not differ from the
base layer.
